<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6409" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">campē</span></b>  (Col. poët. 10, 324; 10,
		366), ēs (the Lat. form of the nom. campa is not
		used), f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάμπη</span>.
			*<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A turning</i>, <i>writhing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">campas dicere,</span>”
				<i>to seek evasions</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Truc. 5, 50</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A caterpillar</i>, pure Lat. eruca, Col. l. l. (cf.
					<i><span class="en">id. 11, 3, 63</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάμπαι</span>); <i><span class="en">Pall. 1,
				35, 6</span></i> and 13.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
